WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.835 --> 00:00:03.335
-Our next guest is a
Tony-nominated actress

00:00:03.402 --> 00:00:04.904
and comedian, you know from
"Saturday Night Live" and movies

00:00:04.971 --> 00:00:06.606
such as "Sisters,"
and "Wine Country."

00:00:06.672 --> 00:00:09.175
Her podcast,
"Woo Woo with Rachel Dratch"

00:00:09.242 --> 00:00:10.609
is available now.

00:00:10.676 --> 00:00:12.879
She also stars in the animated
series "Grimsburg,"

00:00:12.945 --> 00:00:15.748
which returns Sunday,
February 18th at 9:30 on Fox.

00:00:15.814 --> 00:00:17.216
Let's take a look.

00:00:17.283 --> 00:00:18.818
-Don't worry boy, son,
we're going to duct tape

00:00:18.885 --> 00:00:20.153
this broken family back together

00:00:20.219 --> 00:00:22.421
faster than you can say,
hereditary schizophrenia,

00:00:22.488 --> 00:00:24.056
which you also
don't need to worry about

00:00:24.123 --> 00:00:26.826
unless you're still seeing
your imaginary skeleton friend.

00:00:26.893 --> 00:00:28.261
The one who made you pull
the fire alarm.

00:00:28.327 --> 00:00:30.763
-Nope.
Therapy's working great.

00:00:30.830 --> 00:00:32.465
Bye.

00:00:34.634 --> 00:00:36.669
-He bought it, Stanley.

00:00:36.736 --> 00:00:38.004
Now all we got to do
is make sure

00:00:38.071 --> 00:00:40.506
he never talks
to your therapist.

00:00:40.573 --> 00:00:42.341
Just like us.
-Mr. Flesch.

00:00:42.408 --> 00:00:44.077
Now we can finally
start our plan

00:00:44.144 --> 00:00:45.878
to get my parents back together.

00:00:45.945 --> 00:00:47.213
-Please welcome back
to the show,

00:00:47.280 --> 00:00:49.548
our very good friend,
Rachel Dratch.

00:00:49.615 --> 00:00:52.551
[ Cheers and applause ]

