00:08:45.925 --> 00:08:47.226
and that they get back together.

00:08:47.293 --> 00:08:50.096
And it's kind of a sad
yet funny character.

00:08:50.162 --> 00:08:53.365
-Um, I, uh, speaking of kids,
we mentioned backstage

00:08:53.432 --> 00:08:55.935
and say me and my kids,
we walk to school

00:08:56.001 --> 00:08:57.236
and we bump into you
every now and then.

00:08:57.303 --> 00:08:58.804
-Yes, I Bump into Seth
with his kids

00:08:58.870 --> 00:09:00.172
in the morning
when I'm walking my dog.

00:09:00.239 --> 00:09:02.207
-And it's very exciting
because they --

00:09:02.274 --> 00:09:04.276
You did a podcast
which came out a few years ago

00:09:04.343 --> 00:09:06.478
called "The Cinnamon Bear,"
and I highly recommend it.

00:09:06.545 --> 00:09:09.514
It's this wonderful, like,
20 part, uh, Christmas story

00:09:09.581 --> 00:09:11.883
that we listen to when
we road trip over the holidays.

00:09:11.950 --> 00:09:13.218
And so we've listened
to it every year.

00:09:13.285 --> 00:09:15.154
And, uh, they introduce each,

00:09:15.221 --> 00:09:17.790
uh, each episode says
who plays who.

00:09:17.856 --> 00:09:20.393
And it was really exciting
because when we first time

00:09:20.459 --> 00:09:21.793
we ran into you,
I said to my boys, I'm like,

00:09:21.860 --> 00:09:23.429
This is Rachel Dratch
from "Cinnamon Bear."

00:09:23.496 --> 00:09:25.097
And I was like,
who do you play again, Rachel?

00:09:25.164 --> 00:09:26.432
And you were like,
"I have no idea."

00:09:26.499 --> 00:09:28.367
[ Laughter ]

00:09:28.433 --> 00:09:31.603
And my oldest son goes,
"Winnie the Stork."

00:09:31.670 --> 00:09:32.805
And he fully knew your credit.

00:09:32.872 --> 00:09:34.240
-He knew.
-And then you walked away.

00:09:34.306 --> 00:09:35.741
And he was disappointed
that you didn't sound more like

00:09:35.808 --> 00:09:37.143
Winnie the Stork.
-Uh.

00:09:37.209 --> 00:09:39.745
But I thought that
you got home, and he said --

00:09:39.811 --> 00:09:43.316
He said, like,
she sounds just like her.

00:09:43.382 --> 00:09:44.483
Something like that.
-No.

00:09:44.550 --> 00:09:45.851
-Okay, I ruined that.
Cut that lul.

00:09:45.918 --> 00:09:47.286
-Cut that.
-Lul.

00:09:47.352 --> 00:09:49.321
-I definitely want to cut
me getting a story wrong.

00:09:49.388 --> 00:09:50.989
[ Laughter ]

00:09:51.056 --> 00:09:52.491
-Mark that as the second lul.

00:09:52.558 --> 00:09:55.227
[ Laughter ]

00:09:55.294 --> 00:09:56.662
-Okay.
-You know the best thing

00:09:56.729 --> 00:09:58.097
about Tony
nominated actresses, though?

00:09:58.163 --> 00:10:00.032
Even the lulls shine.

00:10:00.099 --> 00:10:02.935
[ Laughter ]

00:10:03.002 --> 00:10:05.270
-Okay.
-Um, yeah.

00:10:05.337 --> 00:10:06.771
-Maybe the audience saw ghost.

00:10:06.838 --> 00:10:08.073
-Maybe.

00:10:08.140 --> 00:10:09.674
-Um, this is weird,
because we're done.

00:10:09.741 --> 00:10:10.843
-Oh. We are?
-Yeah.

00:10:10.910 --> 00:10:12.077
And it's hard to end
on a lull.

00:10:12.143 --> 00:10:14.213
-We're done. Oh, shoot.
Okay, um.

00:10:14.280 --> 00:10:15.781
[ Laughter ]

00:10:15.848 --> 00:10:17.682
-We'll think of something.
-We'll think of something.

00:10:17.749 --> 00:10:18.918
Wait. Are we really done?

00:10:18.984 --> 00:10:20.719
-Yeah, we're kind of done.
-Oh, okay.

00:10:20.786 --> 00:10:22.320
-If you could see any kind of
ghost, what would you see?

00:10:22.387 --> 00:10:25.424
-I got to end on a high note.
-Would you rather hear --

00:10:25.491 --> 00:10:27.859
Would you rather
see a yeti or a mermaid?

00:10:27.926 --> 00:10:29.761
-Ooh, a yeti.
-Really?

00:10:29.828 --> 00:10:31.263
I would so much
rather see a mermaid.

00:10:31.330 --> 00:10:32.331
Really?
Well, because I assume

00:10:32.397 --> 00:10:33.499
in this story I'm in a boat

00:10:33.566 --> 00:10:34.600
and the mermaid can't get me.

00:10:34.667 --> 00:10:36.869
-Okay.
-But if you see a yeti.

00:10:36.935 --> 00:10:38.436
So now you're in the woods
and you see a yeti.

00:10:38.503 --> 00:10:39.671
What are you doing?

00:10:39.738 --> 00:10:41.073
-Well, I'm picturing the yeti

00:10:41.140 --> 00:10:42.507
from "Rudolph the Red-Nosed
Reindeer."

00:10:42.574 --> 00:10:43.843
I'm picturing
Abominable Snowman.

00:10:43.909 --> 00:10:45.677
-Okay, but that's still
a terrifying creature

00:10:45.744 --> 00:10:47.112
before he gets
his dental surgery.

00:10:47.179 --> 00:10:49.982
[ Laughter ]

00:10:52.151 --> 00:10:54.086
-[ Laughs ]

00:10:54.152 --> 00:10:55.688
-You guys, that's Rachel Dratch.

00:10:55.755 --> 00:10:58.891
"Grimsburg" returns
February 18th on Fox,

00:10:58.958 --> 00:11:02.428
and her podcast "Woo Woo" with
Rachel Dratch is available now.

00:11:02.494 --> 00:11:03.929
We'll be right back
with more "Late Night.

